tatement without extra preamble.\n\n", "type": "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Principle: Anchored Umbrella Disease Terms**\n  - **IF** a superordinate disease-category head noun (a broad common noun for a class of conditions, such as a generic inflammatory, infectious, or deficiency term) is **anchored** to one condition, meaning either:\n    - (a) it is the predicate complement of a diagnostic or presentation construction whose subject is a patient or case referent (e.g., \"presenting with ___,\" \"found to have ___,\" \"diagnosed with ___\"), including each member of a coordinated list governed by that construction, or\n    - (b) it carries a premodifier (a gene symbol, a pathogen name, an anatomical site, or another etiology-specifying element) that fixes a single etiology, gene, or site,\n  - **THEN** label the head disease span **SpecificDisease**.\n  - **Otherwise**, if the category noun is unanchored, label it **DiseaseClass**.\n  - **Negative constraint:** Do **not** apply this rule when the category noun appears in a generic or definitional enumeration of features describing a syndrome or phenotype, with no case referent and no etiology-fixing premodifier. Those remain **DiseaseClass**. Descriptive premodifiers that do not identify a cause, gene, or site (e.g., severity, timing, or general evaluative qualifiers) are not anchors. The rule also does not make the premodifier itself a disease mention; the anchor determines only the label of the head disease span.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2141, "output_tokens": 2670, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2187}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}